WEBVTT

00:25.741 --> 00:30.078
FOOL NIGHT

01:44.236 --> 01:48.365
Really, their food is delicious.
Let's go together next time.

01:48.448 --> 01:50.700
I'd love to! What do they have?

01:50.784 --> 01:52.452
They have tons of course options.

01:52.536 --> 01:53.370
RECEPTION OFFICE

01:53.453 --> 01:54.830
Hang on, I have pictures!

01:54.913 --> 01:56.206
I'd love to see them!

01:58.041 --> 02:00.710
Mr. Sakai, what is the meaning of this?

02:01.294 --> 02:03.463
You won't join the Glory Days Party?

02:04.923 --> 02:07.175
We, the anti-transfloration movement,

02:07.259 --> 02:09.469
got you elected with our funding and aid.

02:10.470 --> 02:14.975
It's impossible to abolish
the transfloration policy just like that.

02:15.058 --> 02:17.811
We're going to keep using transfloration

02:17.894 --> 02:20.605
while advancing measures to supply oxygen.

02:23.567 --> 02:25.610
It's all about balance, Hikasa.

02:26.570 --> 02:29.197
Society won't change overnight.

02:32.159 --> 02:33.285
What was that?

02:33.869 --> 02:39.499
Establishing a new political party
requires five core Diet members.

02:40.876 --> 02:42.919
And you're one of them.

02:44.421 --> 02:45.422
Get out.

02:45.505 --> 02:47.632
Don't use me for your publicity stunt.

02:48.383 --> 02:50.927
Why are you doing that? Don't piss me off!

02:51.511 --> 02:53.763
Do you know what this sound means?

03:00.020 --> 03:01.229
How many people

03:02.147 --> 03:04.482
are still alive in this house, I wonder?

03:10.488 --> 03:14.910
The Glory Days Party's press conference
will be underway shortly.

03:21.166 --> 03:24.920
<i>Now, a speech from the Glory Days Party's</i>
<i>Secretary-General Ken Hikasa.</i>

03:36.973 --> 03:38.516
Good morning.

03:38.600 --> 03:40.143
I am Ken Hikasa.

03:42.938 --> 03:45.523
Let's cut to the chase. I'm a liar.

03:48.568 --> 03:53.531
I spent my childhood
with a less-than-wealthy family.

03:54.115 --> 03:57.285
Although we couldn't afford
enough meals or study materials,

03:58.411 --> 04:03.041
our strong family bond
is what kept us together.

04:04.376 --> 04:07.671
But repeated increases in oxygen tax

04:07.754 --> 04:10.423
bled the Hikasa family completely dry.

04:12.050 --> 04:14.052
I hoped that my grandmother

04:14.719 --> 04:17.264
would undergo transfloration for us.

04:18.056 --> 04:19.307
And still,

04:20.642 --> 04:23.311
she continued showering me with love

04:23.395 --> 04:26.940
all the way until complete transfloration.

04:27.023 --> 04:31.820
I wanted to respond
with sincere words of love as well.

04:31.903 --> 04:35.240
But how could I even utter the words,
"I love you"?

04:35.323 --> 04:38.493
Just prior, my heart yearned
for her very death.

04:39.160 --> 04:41.329
This is a lifelong regret of mine.

04:42.414 --> 04:46.960
In a healthy society,
we should never wish death on our family!

04:47.544 --> 04:50.505
Moving forward, we must change!

04:55.093 --> 04:56.970
What's that light for?

04:57.637 --> 04:59.681
The sun is here!

05:00.432 --> 05:03.727
A benevolent sun
shining down on everyone equally!

05:07.188 --> 05:08.857
No more endless nights.

05:09.649 --> 05:11.693
I tell you all, "Good morning."

05:12.360 --> 05:15.989
The Glory Days Party needs your support!

05:21.286 --> 05:22.871
Mr. Hikasa, look over here!

05:22.954 --> 05:27.042
Secretary-General Hikasa,
a word for Koyomi Newspaper, please!

05:27.125 --> 05:29.961
Mr. Hikasa,
regarding your performance just now…

05:30.045 --> 05:33.506
HIKASA & KUDAI

05:43.808 --> 05:44.976
No progress?

05:45.060 --> 05:49.647
Even after all this research,
not a single mention of Dr. Kudai…

05:50.732 --> 05:53.068
We have no choice but to strike first.

05:57.197 --> 05:58.406
HIKASA & KUDAI

05:58.490 --> 06:01.242
We'll lure Hikasa in
using Dr. Kudai's name.

06:01.326 --> 06:03.411
Are we declaring war now?

06:03.495 --> 06:06.998
When Hikasa sees this,
he'll definitely start moving.

06:07.582 --> 06:10.001
I've come prepared with countermeasures.

06:10.585 --> 06:11.795
Holy moly.

06:11.878 --> 06:13.880
This looks fun.

06:14.589 --> 06:18.843
Is there a reason
that you're the one declaring war, Yomiko?

06:19.427 --> 06:22.639
You'll be targeted again, won't you?

06:24.891 --> 06:26.101
You might get killed…

06:27.977 --> 06:28.978
Toshiro.

06:32.190 --> 06:34.317
I swore to protect you.

06:34.400 --> 06:36.277
Transflora Medical, too!

06:36.361 --> 06:37.987
I'm going to kill them all!

06:40.031 --> 06:42.450
Quit being a crybaby. Understand?

06:43.701 --> 06:44.869
Yes, ma'am…

06:50.375 --> 06:52.293
She's a reporter on the press list.

06:54.587 --> 06:55.588
AI AKIYAMA

06:55.672 --> 06:58.842
Before you kill her,
find out what she's trying to extort.

07:05.974 --> 07:09.811
I'll register my name, affiliation,
and address on the event's press list.

07:09.894 --> 07:11.688
A fake name, of course.

07:11.771 --> 07:15.275
And a fake weekly magazine's
third-tier subcontractor as my company.

07:15.358 --> 07:18.528
For my address, I'll rent a room
in a multi-tenant building.

07:18.611 --> 07:19.988
Are you trying to lure them in?

07:20.697 --> 07:22.657
First, we'll capture one of his guards,

07:23.491 --> 07:26.035
interrogate him with Toshiro's ability,

07:26.119 --> 07:28.663
then blackmail him into spying for us.

07:28.746 --> 07:31.082
Only if there are two or fewer guards.

07:31.166 --> 07:33.418
If there are three or more,
abort the mission.

07:41.843 --> 07:43.011
<i>They're here, Kanaeno.</i>

07:43.595 --> 07:44.596
<i>Two of them.</i>

07:45.096 --> 07:46.890
Roger that.

08:20.590 --> 08:21.508
Shit!

08:28.806 --> 08:30.808
Nighty night.

09:09.806 --> 09:14.978
WE PLANTED A SEED INSIDE YOU.

09:17.981 --> 09:23.486
WE SECRETLY DEVELOPED A GROWTH INHIBITOR
WHICH DELAYS THE SEED'S GROWTH.

09:25.572 --> 09:30.743
ANSWER OUR QUESTIONS HONESTLY.
NOD FOR "YES" AND SHAKE FOR "NO".

09:31.327 --> 09:35.498
WE'LL ADMINISTER THE GROWTH INHIBITOR
AFTER YOU ANSWER.

09:42.213 --> 09:44.424
Does a "growth inhibitor" even exist?

09:44.924 --> 09:45.758
Nope.

09:46.342 --> 09:47.802
We're not planting a seed, either.

09:47.885 --> 09:50.638
We'll just open a wound
big enough to feel like a lump.

09:52.140 --> 09:53.850
If he's a member of the opposition,

09:55.101 --> 09:57.854
threatening transfloration
will be enough to break his spirit.

10:01.858 --> 10:04.902
HAVE YOU MET DR. KUDAI?

10:14.954 --> 10:18.791
<i>Panic. Confusion. Animosity.</i>

10:19.626 --> 10:22.003
<i>Sense of duty. Denial.</i>

10:23.630 --> 10:26.215
<i>He's lying. He's met the doctor before.</i>

10:31.137 --> 10:33.473
DID YOU MEET NEAR THIS AREA?

10:35.725 --> 10:36.726
<i>Not lying.</i>

10:37.560 --> 10:39.228
WHAT ABOUT HERE?

10:40.813 --> 10:42.231
HERE?

10:45.902 --> 10:47.779
Stop, you're asking too much.

10:48.446 --> 10:50.740
When the mind lies too much,
I can't read anymore.

10:52.950 --> 10:58.998
IS KEN HIKASA COMMANDING
TEN OR MORE INTELLIGENCE AGENTS?

11:01.459 --> 11:02.502
<i>He's lying.</i>

11:02.585 --> 11:03.795
<i>It's more than ten.</i>

11:06.089 --> 11:07.590
<i>The second party is here.</i>

11:07.674 --> 11:09.008
<i>Way earlier than expected!</i>

11:09.092 --> 11:11.386
<i>We were supposed to leave</i>
<i>before they arrived!</i>

11:14.347 --> 11:17.975
YOU WON'T GET THE GROWTH INHIBITOR YET.

11:18.059 --> 11:21.396
YOU HAVE THREE DAYS TO GET INFO ON KUDAI.

11:26.442 --> 11:27.902
What are you doing? Hurry up!

11:30.363 --> 11:31.280
Is Ivy…

11:32.281 --> 11:33.282
still alive?

12:09.485 --> 12:10.695
What now, Nishi?

12:11.487 --> 12:14.240
Should I storm in and kill everybody?

12:15.199 --> 12:16.200
No.

12:16.284 --> 12:18.911
We don't know what sort of traps
they've set for us.

12:19.495 --> 12:21.497
Harubara, climb the adjacent building

12:21.581 --> 12:24.417
and jump onto the target building's roof.

12:24.500 --> 12:27.420
We'll sandwich them from above and below.

12:31.299 --> 12:32.675
Kanaeno's fast!

12:58.201 --> 12:59.368
<i>Gunshot?</i>

13:02.538 --> 13:03.956
They're quick.

13:06.042 --> 13:08.336
<i>I should've beaten them here.</i>

13:32.193 --> 13:33.402
You're good.

13:36.989 --> 13:40.326
Can't shoot without this?

13:42.370 --> 13:44.038
Bye-bye.

13:50.920 --> 13:51.921
Go!

13:52.922 --> 13:55.424
You're bleeding like hell! Are you okay?

13:55.508 --> 13:56.759
Just drive!

13:56.842 --> 13:58.010
Yeah, drive…

14:09.063 --> 14:10.064
Akira…

14:13.818 --> 14:14.944
It won't come off.

14:15.027 --> 14:16.737
I can't cut it, either.

14:16.821 --> 14:21.033
They knew about Dr. Kudai and Ivy.

14:21.701 --> 14:24.203
They also asked the number of our agents

14:24.287 --> 14:26.330
and Dr. Kudai's specific location.

14:26.414 --> 14:28.749
Of course, I kept my mouth shut.

14:28.833 --> 14:31.752
What happened to your party badge?

14:33.045 --> 14:34.630
It should be inside my collar.

14:35.214 --> 14:36.340
If not, they stole it.

14:37.300 --> 14:38.885
Okay, that's fine.

14:39.468 --> 14:42.555
Your corpse won't lead them
to the Glory Days Party.

14:42.638 --> 14:43.639
What?

14:47.184 --> 14:50.271
Since we can't move you,
you'll just have to die.

14:51.188 --> 14:52.690
What now, Nishi?

14:53.399 --> 14:55.526
Cut him into four pieces and take him out?

14:56.110 --> 14:58.988
With that knife,
it would take two or three hours.

14:59.906 --> 15:04.035
If we'd let that monster slice him up,
it would've been over in a flash.

15:04.911 --> 15:05.953
Let's just go.

15:06.662 --> 15:08.039
I know who the enemy is.

15:09.707 --> 15:12.293
Abolish transfloration!

15:13.377 --> 15:15.463
Abolish transfloration!

15:16.130 --> 15:18.633
Abolish transfloration!

15:19.383 --> 15:21.302
Don't let them do this!

15:21.385 --> 15:24.680
That monster killed our son!

15:31.896 --> 15:34.440
I heard you borrowed
Kunibe's mercenary unit.

15:35.274 --> 15:37.443
Now that we know Ivy's alive,

15:37.526 --> 15:39.695
we can't just roam around unarmed.

15:40.696 --> 15:42.949
The protests are getting
more violent, too.

15:43.658 --> 15:47.828
To promptly track down Dr. Kudai,
we need powerful pieces.

15:48.412 --> 15:51.374
I can't believe you persuaded that Kunibe.

15:52.166 --> 15:55.002
A member of the Glory Days Party
succumbed to his conscience

15:55.711 --> 15:58.839
and secretly leaked the details
of Ivy's creation to us.

15:58.923 --> 16:03.844
So they killed him to shut him up.
That's the story I presented to Kunibe.

16:04.720 --> 16:09.100
When I submitted the party member's corpse
and Ivy's bedsheet as proof of the leak,

16:09.183 --> 16:10.309
he believed me.

16:11.352 --> 16:15.356
Because, without a leak,
we'd never find evidence like that.

16:15.439 --> 16:20.611
Basically, you waited for the right moment
to show the evidence Toshiro brought back.

16:20.695 --> 16:23.739
He was elated to find out
that Ivy was still alive.

16:24.657 --> 16:26.909
He's willing to help us in other ways too.

16:28.077 --> 16:31.497
We're lucky that the opposition
killed one of their own this time.

16:32.248 --> 16:34.875
That made our story more convincing.

16:35.501 --> 16:37.753
Wasn't this your goal all along?

16:39.046 --> 16:42.383
You never intended
to make the hostage guy spy for us.

16:43.342 --> 16:44.885
You knew he'd be killed.

16:47.221 --> 16:49.306
Did you just read my emotions?

16:49.390 --> 16:50.391
No.

16:51.017 --> 16:52.643
I don't want to use my ability on you.

16:53.352 --> 16:55.980
He only died
because they were being brutal.

16:58.441 --> 17:00.192
Now that we've partnered with Kunibe,

17:01.360 --> 17:03.154
what's gonna happen to Ivy?

17:03.237 --> 17:04.280
We'll hand Ivy over.

17:04.780 --> 17:07.033
As payment for lending us
the mercenary unit.

17:07.992 --> 17:09.618
He'll be a guinea pig until he dies.

17:11.120 --> 17:12.455
Why are you so shocked?

17:13.247 --> 17:15.249
Why do you feel bad for Ivy?

17:15.332 --> 17:17.251
He nearly killed me, you know.

17:17.334 --> 17:20.629
He tried to kill Deputy Chief Yatsuka,
Kanaeno, and even you.

17:21.589 --> 17:24.633
On top of that,
he's killed dozens of civilians.

17:27.553 --> 17:31.015
No amount of sympathy could
make up for what he's done.

17:34.101 --> 17:35.102
I'm leaving.

17:43.319 --> 17:44.820
Welcome back, sir.

17:46.822 --> 17:48.824
You've received a letter.

17:51.160 --> 17:53.287
HOUSE OF LOVE
SASAKI ORPHANAGE

17:53.370 --> 17:57.208
THANK YOU, MISTER!
FROM YOKO HIKITA

18:15.726 --> 18:17.353
<i>Our enemy is Transflora Medical.</i>

18:19.313 --> 18:21.440
What do they want to know?

18:22.149 --> 18:25.736
Mainly about Dr. Kudai and Ivy, I suppose.

18:25.820 --> 18:27.947
They asked for specific locations.

18:29.031 --> 18:31.492
Both of them must be guarded.

18:32.201 --> 18:33.828
Where's Ivy now?

18:34.411 --> 18:36.622
In recovery under Dr. Kudai's care.

18:37.790 --> 18:41.418
But a time will come
when he must act for the world's sake.

18:41.502 --> 18:43.963
We must be grateful
for his noble sacrifice.

18:45.422 --> 18:48.425
How did your connection
to Dr. Kudai get leaked?

18:48.509 --> 18:49.510
I don't know.

18:50.010 --> 18:51.887
I'd love to visit Dr. Kudai

18:51.971 --> 18:53.722
and ask him myself,

18:53.806 --> 18:55.975
but now they're spying on me.

18:56.058 --> 18:57.268
Spying?

18:57.351 --> 18:59.436
Is that why you wanted to talk here?

18:59.520 --> 19:00.688
Exactly.

19:00.771 --> 19:04.942
The doorstop in my study had moved
since I last left.

19:05.734 --> 19:08.904
<i>They're too far away.</i>
<i>I have no clue what's happening.</i>

19:10.030 --> 19:12.825
If I approach Dr. Kudai,
they'll discover his location.

19:13.701 --> 19:16.954
If you're stuck here, Mr. Hikasa,
should my team go meet him instead?

19:18.372 --> 19:20.332
Your team could never find him.

19:21.083 --> 19:23.085
In order to contact the doctor,

19:23.169 --> 19:26.964
I use a dedicated line
to exchange meeting times and coordinates.

19:27.047 --> 19:29.633
And then I meet him directly.
That's our deal.

19:30.676 --> 19:34.513
If Dr. Kudai is communicating
with Transflora Medical somehow

19:34.597 --> 19:37.099
and we can't ask the doctor about it,

19:37.725 --> 19:39.393
there's only one place to investigate.

19:40.186 --> 19:42.104
Transflora Medical.

19:43.397 --> 19:44.565
Exactly.

19:46.025 --> 19:47.026
One question.

19:47.776 --> 19:49.987
Could you disclose some information

19:50.070 --> 19:53.741
from before the doctor's disappearance
that hasn't been made public?

19:54.325 --> 19:56.952
That would make it
much easier to infiltrate.

19:57.828 --> 20:00.289
I'm well aware that all information

20:00.372 --> 20:03.667
surrounding Dr. Kudai is classified, but…

20:07.296 --> 20:10.007
Dr. Kudai worked in Antarctica.

20:11.383 --> 20:14.011
Damn it! You're full of shit!

20:14.887 --> 20:16.805
Oppose transfloration!

20:16.889 --> 20:19.266
You created that monster!

20:27.149 --> 20:29.568
KAORI & TOSHIRO KAMIYA

20:41.413 --> 20:43.249
<i>Born in Paupertown…</i>

20:45.542 --> 20:47.628
<i>Out in the cold wind,</i>

20:48.170 --> 20:49.672
<i>earning meager daily payments…</i>

20:51.131 --> 20:53.300
<i>Having his only family taken away…</i>

20:54.426 --> 20:55.302
SHIIKA

20:55.386 --> 20:58.222
<i>…and killed to become</i>
<i>a silly piece of furniture.</i>

21:00.849 --> 21:01.850
<i>He finally…</i>

21:03.394 --> 21:05.813
<i>He finally escaped Paupertown, but now…</i>

21:08.774 --> 21:10.484
<i>If Transflora Medical catches him,</i>

21:11.277 --> 21:13.362
<i>he'll be their guinea pig forever.</i>

21:14.071 --> 21:15.406
<i>But if we leave him alone,</i>

21:16.115 --> 21:18.075
<i>Ivy will go on another killing spree.</i>

21:20.077 --> 21:21.078
It's awful.

21:22.705 --> 21:25.916
No amount of sympathy
could make up for what he's done.

21:27.459 --> 21:28.460
<i>I know that.</i>

21:29.712 --> 21:32.089
<i>He needs to face the consequences. I know.</i>

21:33.799 --> 21:34.883
<i>I know that.</i>

21:35.467 --> 21:36.885
<i>I get it!</i>

21:38.137 --> 21:39.388
<i>I get it.</i>

21:41.974 --> 21:43.392
Ivy…

21:44.977 --> 21:46.186
<i>You're the only one</i>

21:46.687 --> 21:48.147
<i>I've been able to talk to.</i>

22:08.042 --> 22:09.043
<i>Me…</i>

22:11.253 --> 22:12.254
<i>It's gotta be me.</i>

22:14.673 --> 22:15.674
<i>I have to…</i>

22:16.925 --> 22:18.302
<i>put him out of his misery.</i>

23:46.932 --> 23:51.937
Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins
